# THE SCRIPTS THE SYSTEM EXECUTES ARE LF, WHATEVER THE CHECKOUT.
#
# sh reads a CRLF script and hands the shell options with a \r stuck to them:
# util/setup/install.sh died on Linux with "set: Illegal option -" because a
# Windows checkout converted its line endings on the way out. eol=lf pins the
# working tree copy too, so what runs is what git holds.
*.sh text eol=lf
